semsplit is an independent re-implementation. Its default behaviour and constructor
arguments are compatible with `SemanticChunker` from langchain-experimental
(https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain-experimental, MIT License, archived 2026-05-22),
whose algorithm comes from Greg Kamradt's "5 Levels Of Text Splitting" notebook
(https://github.com/FullStackRetrieval-com/RetrievalTutorials).

tests/golden/semantic_chunker_0.4.2.json holds the output of langchain-experimental 0.4.2
for the inputs listed in the file; it is recorded data, not code.

